sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Since a universal cellular automaton exists, any type of system shown capable of emulating any cellular automaton—including mobile automata, Turing machines, neighbor-dependent and sequential substitution systems, tag systems, cyclic tag systems, symbolic systems and register machines—must contain universal examples.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Any system type that can emulate every cellular automaton has universal members";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “Emulating Cellular Automata with Other Systems” (from p. 664), p. 668. Scope: mobile automata, Turing machines, substitution systems, tag and cyclic tag systems, symbolic systems, register machines"
}
